  "prefLabel": "Res 5901.05 Conviction of Laws of Another State",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Res 5901.05 Conviction of Laws of Another State. If a person is convicted under the laws of another state, of a law that contains the same elements as any offense listed under Res 5901.02 (b), the conviction shall be used for the purpose of assessing points for an enhanced penalty.\n\nSource. #10547, eff 3-21-14",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res5200-5900.html"
